{"id": "tea:muktivada-raghudeva:opening", "source": "src:muktivada-raghudeva", "location": {"ref": "opening"}, "paraphrase": "The Ācāryas (Udayana) say that liberation is the absolute cessation of pain; its absoluteness is its not being contemporaneous with any prior absence of pain in the same locus — i.e. liberation is a destruction of pain not contemporaneous with any prior absence of pain in the same self.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "original": {"text": "ātyantikī duḥkhanivṛttir muktir ity ācāryāḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Navyanyāyavādagranthāḥ (Delhi Sanskrit Academy 2008), raw_etexts", "licence": "see repository"}, "speaker": "Raghudeva", "terms": ["trm:mukti", "trm:duhkha", "trm:pragabhava", "trm:pradhvamsabhava"], "concepts": ["cpt:apavarga-nyaya"], "teachers": ["tch:udayana"], "disputes": ["dsp:bliss-in-liberation"], "notes": "Checked against the local e-text.", "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U11-nyaya-vaisesika"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U11-nyaya-vaisesika"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
